.TH SKYBOX-THUMBS 1 "2026-10-25" "skybox-thumbs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skybox-thumbs \- pre-generate SKYBOX custom thumbnails as sidecar JPEGs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skybox-thumbs
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIDIR\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skybox-thumbs
scans video folders and writes a JPEG next to every video, using the same
basename with a
.B .jpg
extension (for example
.I clip.ts
and
.IR clip.jpg ).
SKYBOX uses such an image as the custom thumbnail of the video, including
when the video is reached over SMB, and therefore no longer has to download
and decode a frame for every file when a folder is opened.
.P
This matters most for large VR captures: the 5760\(mu2880 HEVC MPEG-TS files
in this collection take roughly half a second and tens of megabytes of network
traffic each to sample on the headset, over hundreds of files. Sidecar images
are a few kilobytes and are read directly from the share.
.P
The sampled frame is taken at
.B \-\-percent
of the duration (default 15), clamped to between
.B \-\-min\-offset
(default 30 seconds) and
.B \-\-max\-offset
(default 600 seconds). Frames are written as 640\(mu640
bounding-box JPEGs at
.B \-\-quality
4 (roughly 15\-25 kB each).
.P
Seeking in these MPEG-TS captures frequently decodes to a flat grey frame, so
extraction uses
.BR ffmpeg (1)
with
.B \-skip_frame nokey
and starts at a keyframe. If the result is suspiciously small (under 4096
bytes), or extraction fails, the first keyframe is tried and the larger image
is kept. A video that yields no image at all is reported and skipped; it does
not abort the run.
.P
Without positional arguments the directories default to
.I vr
and
.I Good
under the first existing of
.I /mnt/pve/Data_Storage
(the Proxmox host, where the files are local) and
.IR /mnt/data_storage .
The script is normally run on the Proxmox host; from a workstation use
.BR skybox-thumbs-remote (1).
.P
On the Proxmox host a systemd timer
.RI ( skybox-thumbs.timer )
runs the script every three hours (00:00, 03:00, and so on) with a randomised
delay of up to 10 minutes. A systemd user timer of the same name does the same
on the workstation for
.IR /mnt/shared/VR ,
which is an NTFS disk that only exists there; that timer passes the path
explicitly. The service processes one video at a time at idle
I/O priority and low CPU weight. It checks for an existing sidecar before
doing anything else and skips that video, so a run with nothing new only lists
directories and calls
.BR stat (2):
it reads no video data, starts no
.B ffmpeg
process and writes nothing. New recordings get their sidecar at the next run;
run
.B skybox-thumbs
manually to cover them sooner.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-j " N, \-\-jobs " N
Extract up to
.I N
thumbnails in parallel. Default: 2. Every
.B ffmpeg
and
.B ffprobe
process is run with
.B nice
19 and
.B ionice
class 3.
.TP
.BI \-p " PCT, \-\-percent " PCT
Sample the frame this percentage into the video. Default: 15.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-offset " SEC"
Never sample earlier than
.I SEC
seconds. Default: 30.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-offset " SEC"
Never sample later than
.I SEC
seconds. Default: 600.
.TP
.BI \-w " PX, \-\-width " PX
Thumbnail bounding box, preserving aspect ratio. Default: 640.
.TP
.BI \-q " N, \-\-quality " N
.B ffmpeg
.B \-q:v
value for the JPEG encoder, 2 (best) to 31 (worst). Default: 4.
.TP
.BI \-t " SEC, \-\-timeout " SEC
Per-video
.B ffmpeg
timeout. Default: 180 seconds.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be created or pruned; write nothing.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Regenerate sidecars that already exist.
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Delete orphaned
.B .jpg
sidecars: only files whose names match the ctbrec recording pattern and that
have no matching video in the same directory. Other images are never touched.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recursive
Scan only the top level of each directory instead of descending.
.TP
.BI \-l " N, \-\-limit " N
Process at most
.I N
videos. Useful for a pilot run.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress per-file output; the summary and failures are still printed.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Also print videos skipped because a sidecar already exists.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS Output
.IP \(bu 2
A sidecar is written next to its video as
.IR name.jpg ,
atomically via a hidden temporary file, so an interrupted run never leaves a
partial image.
.IP \(bu 2
The sidecar inherits the video's owner, group and permission bits (with the
group-write bit added), so SMB clients can read it.
.IP \(bu 2
Videos that already have
.BR .jpg ,
.B .jpeg
or
.B .png
sidecar are skipped unless
.B \-\-force
is given. Exit status is 1 if any video failed.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.B ffmpeg
and
.B ffprobe
on
.IR PATH .
.IP \(bu 2
Enough free space for roughly 25 kB per video.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate thumbnails for the default folders on the Proxmox host:
.IP
.EX
skybox-thumbs
.EE
.P
Pilot three files, then inspect them in the headset:
.IP
.EX
skybox-thumbs \-\-limit 3
.EE
.P
Regenerate everything in two folders in parallel:
.IP
.EX
skybox-thumbs \-\-force \-j 3 /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/vr /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/Good
.EE
.P
Same, from a workstation, over SSH:
.IP
.EX
skybox-thumbs-remote \-\-force \-j 3
.EE
.P
Remove sidecars whose videos have been deleted:
.IP
.EX
skybox-thumbs \-\-prune
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All requested thumbnails exist (or would be created, with
.BR \-\-dry\-run ).
.TP
.B 1
At least one video could not be sampled, or an argument or dependency was
invalid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <video>.jpg
Generated thumbnail, same folder and basename as the video.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/skybox-thumbs.timer
Three-hourly schedule on the Proxmox host (00:00, 03:00, ... with up to 10 minutes of jitter).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/skybox-thumbs.service
One-shot service running this script with idle I/O priority.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/skybox-thumbs.timer
Three-hourly user timer on the workstation for
.IR /mnt/shared/VR .
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/skybox-thumbs.service
User service invoked by that timer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skybox-thumbs-remote (1),
.BR ctbrec-vr (1),
.BR ctbrec-vr-remote (1),
.BR ts2mkv (1),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
